\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Sow in the morn thy seed,
\par At eve hold not thine hand;
\par To doubt and fear give thou no heed,
\par Broadcast it o'er the land.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Beside all waters sow,
\par The highway furrows stock,
\par Drop it where thorns and thistles grow,
\par Scatter it on the rock.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The good, the fruitful ground,
\par Expect here nor there;
\par O'er hill and dale, by plots 'tis found
\par Go forth, then, everywhere.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And duly shall appear,
\par In verdure, beauty, strength,
\par The tender blade, the stalk, the ear,
\par And the full corn at length.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thou canst not toil in vain;
\par Cold, heat, and moist, and dry,
\par Shall foster and mature the grain
\par For garners in the sky.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Thence, when the glorious end,
\par The day of God is come,
\par The angels reapear shall descend,
\par And heaven cry: Harvest home!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

